#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Check 3 of .githooks/pre-push used to demand that EVERY outgoing
# commit — author and committer — carry the project identity. That is right for the
# maintainer's own commits and wrong for everyone else's: it refused every external
# contribution outright. It blocked the merge of PR #13 and PR #22 on 2026-08-08, and it
# could not have been worked around locally, because a push of any branch built on main
# also carries the contributor commits already in main's history.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT DO. This is NOT a relaxation to "any identity passes". The gate is still
# DEFAULT DENY: an identity that is not the project identity and not listed here still
# refuses the push. Adding a line is a deliberate act, which is the point — an unexpected
# author is exactly the signal worth stopping on.
#
# THE MAINTAINER'S OTHER IDENTITY CAN NEVER BE ADMITTED HERE. The hook reads it from the
# machine's global gitconfig at runtime and denies it BEFORE consulting this file, so no
# entry below can re-admit it. That ordering is deliberate; do not reverse it. The private
# value is never written into this repo — the repo is public.
#
# The content scrub (check 4) still runs over every contributor commit's metadata, message
# and added lines. Being listed here buys an identity nothing except the right to appear as
# an author.
#
# This gate is about WHOSE NAME is on a commit, never about whether the code is any good.
# Contributed code still goes through PR review, CI, cargo-deny and the licence/NOTICE
# guard. Do not read a name here as "this person's patches are pre-approved".
#
# These addresses are already public in the commit metadata of this repo's history; listing
# them here exposes nothing new. One email per line, # starts a comment.

